        "text": "Hebrew: 'five and thirty years.'",
        "reason": "lexical_alternative"
      },
      {
        "marker": "b",
        "text": "Or 'became the father of Shelah'; traditional English: 'begot Shelah.'",
        "reason": "lexical_alternative"
      },
      {
        "marker": "c",
        "text": "Some traditions render the name as 'Salah.'",
        "reason": "alternative_reading"
      },
      {
        "marker": "d",
        "text": "The Masoretic text, followed here, makes Arpachshad father Shelah at 35. The Greek text printed by Rahlfs–Hanhart instead gives Arpachshad 135 at Cainan's birth, then Cainan 130 at Shelah's birth (Greek verse 13). The Samaritan text printed by Tal and Florentin directly connects Arpachshad and Shelah but gives Arpachshad 135. The traditions also differ in the subsequent years and other ages in this genealogy.",
        "reason": "textual_variant"
      }
    ]
  },
  "lexical_decisions": [
