      "lexicon": "HALOT",
      "rationale": "יַלַד in genealogies commonly means 'to father/beget.' 'Fathered' is more natural modern English than 'begot' while remaining more precise than the weaker 'had.'"
    },
    {
      "source_word": "אֶת",
      "chosen": "[not separately translated]",
      "lexicon": "HALOT",
      "rationale": "אֶת marks the definite direct object in Hebrew and normally has no direct English equivalent; its function is represented by English word order."
